{{- define "custom.custom.configuration.header" -}}
## Custom configuration
{{- end -}}

{{- define "custom.custom.configuration" -}}
{{ template "custom.custom.configuration.header" . }}

[ha-to-tn-reporter](https://github.com/egeback/ha-to-tn-reporter) reads
temperature sensors from Home Assistant and reports them to
[temperatur.nu](https://www.temperatur.nu). Several sensors can feed one
station; they are aggregated.

```yaml
controllers:
  main:
    containers:
      main:
        env:
          REPORTER_HA_URL: http://home-assistant.home.svc:8123
          REPORTER_SENSOR_MAPPING: mystation=sensor.outside_north|sensor.outside_south

reporter:
  existingSecret: ha-tn-reporter   # keys: REPORTER_HA_TOKEN, REPORTER_TN_HASH

persistence:
  data:
    enabled: true
```

Set `REPORTER_MQTT_HOST` to publish the reporter's state to Home Assistant via
MQTT discovery. With MQTT enabled, `/health` (and so the probes) also requires
a working MQTT connection.
{{- end -}}
